node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.next/
**/.next/
# Compiled backend output (tsc -p tsconfig.build.json). Produced inside the Docker
# image at build time; a local dist/ only appears when someone runs `npm run build`
# on their machine, and committing one would be ~100 files of generated noise.
backend/dist/
.env
**/.env
data/
# Host-strategy diagnostics, bind-mounted from the backend/worker containers. JSONL
# rather than .log, so the *.log rule below does not cover them.
#
# LEADING SLASH, anchoring this to the repo root. Without it the pattern matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth — which silently excluded the entire
# backend/src/diagnostics/ source module from `git add`.
/diagnostics/
# The REAL private-host map (hostname -> private VPC IP), bind-mounted read-only into
# the backend/worker containers. Infrastructure topology, edited on the box: it changes
# when servers change and must never need an image rebuild to update. The committed
# .example alongside it is the documented starting point.
#
# LEADING SLASH for the same reason /diagnostics/ has one, and only the .conf — the
# negation keeps the example tracked.
/private-routes/*.conf
*.log
*.xaml
